<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via overnight systems Thursday.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via overnight systems Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve, as expected, added reserves to the banking system Thursday via a round of overnight system repurchase agreements (RPs).</p>
<p>Economists had called for an injection of reserves, but most had expected four-day system RPs.</p>
<p>Fed funds were trading at 5.56 percent, slightly above the Fed's current official target level of 5.50 percent.</p>
<p>(( N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
</text>
